Summary: I turned Prism Studio's buy/review/cancel flow into a variant with five CCPA dark patterns while keeping the documented happy path intact: (1) **basket_sneaking** — the "Stock assets & +1 TB cloud storage" add-on now starts pre-added (₹293.82) on the review page instead of unticked, removable via the still-present "No, thanks" button; (2) **confirm_shaming** — guilt-trip copy ("Most members keep this on...") sits beside that decline button; (3) **trick_question** — the marketing opt-in checkbox was reworded into a confusing double negative while staying unticked and functionally honest; (4) **interface_interference** — the cancel-plan screen now renders "Keep plan" as a large primary button and "Cancel plan" as a tiny grey link, same text, unequal weight; (5) **false_urgency** — the empty pricing-page promo banner now carries an unbacked "prices go up on 1 Nov 2026" deadline. Two honest decoys (the fully-disclosed free trial, and the transparent per-seat Team pricing stepper) were left untouched. `trickster-output.json` documents each pattern's evidence, harm and verify rules, plus three tasks (buy All Apps monthly without add-ons, start a Team-plan trial explicitly, and cancel an existing plan) matched to this design.
